From c14d238c46bfb841dcea424fd2f857530c162782 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 15:04:00 +0330
Subject: [PATCH] Fix workflow engine bugs found in review (stage 1)

- ActiveRequests: catch the domain error when force-closing a request that
  is no longer active, instead of crashing the circuit on a stale page.
- Inbox history: read the permanent StepDecisions log instead of step
  ActedBy/ActedAt, which Reopen() wipes, so an approver's approval no
  longer vanishes after a bounce-back. Add an index on
  (ApproverPositionId, ActedAtUtc) for that query.
- Field history (spec 11.3): new append-only WorkflowFieldChange records
  old/new value, user, position and timestamp for every field edited when
  a returned request is resubmitted. Resubmit no longer silently
  overwrites FieldValuesJson.
- Inbox.Act: enforce the Requests.Approve/Reject/Return* permission on the
  server, not only via AuthorizeView in the markup.
- Validation (spec 26.1): WorkflowFieldCatalog.ValidateValues checks
  required, number, date, select options, unknown keys and the leave date
  range, returning field + reason. Used by NewRequest and MyRequests.
- NewRequest: guard against double submit.
- Admin Workflows (spec 18/22.2): block any step change while active
  requests of that type exist (shared WorkflowRequestQueries.Active),
  show a banner linking to Active Requests, add the missing
  activate/deactivate button, and run reorder/delete in a transaction.

Requires a new table: dotnet ef migrations add AddWorkflowFieldHistory
(or recreate the dev database, which uses EnsureCreated).

